    "peerReview": "The current implementation relies on in-memory state, meaning all habit data will be lost upon configuration changes like screen rotation; you should integrate Room database or DataStore to persist user data effectively. From an architectural standpoint, the UI logic and data state are tightly coupled in the HabitTrackerScreen; consider extracting the input UI into a separate stateless composable to improve maintainability and testability. Additionally, the app lacks a feedback mechanism or state management for empty lists, such as a placeholder illustration or text, which would significantly improve the UX. Finally, ensure you define a consistent color scheme using dynamic colors or custom themes rather than hardcoded Material defaults to ensure accessibility and professional visual parity."
