    "peerReview": "The current implementation suffers from significant audio latency and synchronization issues because multiple concurrent coroutines are attempting to write to a single shared AudioTrack instance; this creates race conditions and buffer starvation. To improve performance, you should adopt an additive synthesis model where a single loop mixes all active waveforms into one buffer before calling write once per cycle, or transition to the Oboe C++ library for low-latency native audio processing. Furthermore, moving audio logic out of the Activity into a dedicated Service or a long-lived AudioEngine class would better adhere to Android lifecycle best practices, preventing audio cut-offs during configuration changes. Finally, ensure the UI layer supports multi-touch; your current pointerInput implementation only tracks a single interaction at a time, limiting the app to monophonic playback."
