    "peerReview": "The current architecture tightly couples sound playback to the Activity lifecycle via MediaPlayer, which risks memory leaks and playback issues if the activity is recreated; consider moving sound management to a dedicated SoundEffectManager or using a simpler Compose-friendly effect handler. From a UX perspective, the timer logic uses a hardcoded loop that lacks pause/resume capability and is prone to drift; I recommend using a more robust time-tracking approach using SystemClock to ensure accuracy. Finally, the UI lacks configuration persistence, so color changes and timer states will reset on screen rotation; utilize SavedStateHandle in your ViewModel to maintain state across configuration changes and provide a smoother user experience."
